Through the catacombs you must pass. Not long ago, the one called Galahad entered the catacombs and has not returned. If you are ready to follow him, ask of me "open the catacombs", and I will do so.	你必須穿過地下墓窖。不久前，那位喚作葛拉漢的騎士已進入地下墓窖，至今未歸。你若已準備好追隨他而去，便向我說「open the catacombs」，我自當為你開啟通路。
I am the hierophant you seek, King Arthur. Though I may admit you to face the next Guardian of the Sacred Cup, you have not yet passed the Test of Symbols.	我便是你所尋的祭司，亞瑟王。雖然我可讓你去面對下一位聖杯守護者，但你尚未通過符號考驗。
Unless you do, you face almost certain death in the catacombs. This may be the fate of Galahad, who entered without heeding my warning. He has not been seen again.	若不如此，你在地下墓窖中幾乎必死無疑。葛拉漢或許正是如此下場——他無視我的警告便逕自進入，此後再無人見過他。
Return to Fatima and complete the Test. But if you choose to ignore this warning, say to me "Open the catacombs" and I will let you pass.	回到法提瑪那裡完成考驗吧。但你若執意無視這個警告，便向我說「Open the catacombs」，我便放你通行。
You would ask a gift from a poor leprous beggar?	你竟向一個貧苦的痲瘋乞丐討要禮物？
Return to Fatima and pass the Test of Symbols, if you desire greater help from me.	你若盼望從我這裡得到更多的援助，就回到法提瑪那裡通過符號考驗吧。
Your reward for such a mean-spirited action would be to burn your hands.	如此刻薄的行徑，換來的報應就是燒傷你的雙手。
Usually an alm can be money, though sometimes it may be some other gift. You must decide what would be best to give this beggar.	施捨通常是錢財，但有時也可以是別的餽贈。你得自行判斷，什麼才是給這位乞丐最好的東西。
Bless you! May you always walk the path of righteousness.	願上天保佑你！願你永遠行走在正義之路上。
Bless you, good sir, bless you!	願上天保佑你，善心的大人，願上天保佑你！
May you be richly blessed for your kindness!	願你的善心得到豐厚的福報！
Best to leave it to the beggar to decide when and how to burn the charcoal once you give it to him.	木炭一旦交給了這位乞丐，何時、如何燃燒，最好還是留給他自己決定。
Great is your charity, yet I would only ask for one thing -- a bag of charcoal.	你的仁慈可謂深厚，但我只求一件事——一袋木炭。
I am content with what I have.	我對現有的一切已心滿意足。
I am but a poor, leprous beggar, not a merchant.	我不過是個貧苦的痲瘋乞丐，並非商人。
It is not mine to give.	此物並非我所能給予。
There are many merchants in the bazaar who may help you, though they will not help me.	市集裡有許多商人或許能幫得上你，只是他們不會幫我。
My task it to guide you toward the Grail, nothing more.	我的任務只是指引你尋向聖杯，僅此而已。
What answer can you expect from a leprous beggar?	你能從一個痲瘋乞丐那裡得到什麼答案呢？
He chose to enter the catacombs without passing the Test of Symbols. He has not been seen since.	他未通過符號考驗便執意進入地下墓窖，自此再無人見過他。
If you ask me to open the catacombs, then I will tell you more. If you choose not to enter, there is no point in my telling you anything.	你若要我開啟地下墓窖，我便會告訴你更多。你若不打算進入，那我說再多也是枉然。
Wisdom and knowledge must always be sought. With them you will be rewarded, but without them you will be doomed.	智慧與知識永遠值得追求。擁有它們，你將得到回報；缺了它們，你便注定沉淪。
She is extremely powerful for she has the highest favor of the goddess.	她法力極為強大，因為她最受女神的眷顧。
Once in this city she was greatly worshipped under the name of Aphrodite. By that name still we call her.	昔日在這座城裡，她曾以阿芙羅黛蒂之名備受敬奉，至今我們仍如此稱呼她。
Tamra serves Aphrodite, as do I.	泰姆拉侍奉阿芙羅黛蒂，我也是。
I sit with by back to the north, my face to the south, half in shadow, half in light.	我坐著，背朝北方，面向南方，半身隱於陰影，半身沐於光中。
Thanks to your generosity, the charcoal will keep me warm during the cold nights.	多虧你的慷慨，這些木炭能讓我在寒夜裡保持溫暖。
The burning charcoal heats my brazier which in turn warms my poor diseased body.	燃燒的木炭溫暖了我的火盆，火盆又溫暖了我這副可憐病弱的身軀。
My brazier needs charcoal to keep me warm during the cold nights.	我的火盆需要木炭，才能讓我在寒夜裡保持溫暖。
It causes my body to rot, my fingers and toes to fall off. Do not come near me, I beg you.	這病使我的身軀腐爛，手指與腳趾一根根脫落。求你別靠近我。
I guard the way to the catacombs and admit only those who are found worthy.	我看守著通往地下墓窖的道路，只放行被認定為夠格之人。
No thief dares to rob from a leper.	沒有哪個竊賊敢向痲瘋病人下手。
Bless you a thousand times, good sir! May your charity win you a place in Paradise.	千謝萬謝，善心的大人！願你的慈悲為你換得天國的一席之地。
Because you have passed the Test of Symbols, I will give you a gift that could save your life. Within the catacombs are cursed rats whose bite is poison.	既然你已通過符號考驗，我便贈你一件能救你性命之物。地下墓窖裡棲居著受詛咒的老鼠，牠們的咬傷帶有劇毒。
One bite from these rats and you will die slowly. Even the slightest bite means certain death. If bitten again, the end comes more quickly and with great agony.	被這些老鼠咬上一口，你便會緩緩死去。哪怕只是輕輕一咬，也必死無疑。若再遭二次咬傷，死期便會加速降臨，且痛苦萬分。
Take this vial of elixir.	收下這瓶解藥吧。
As you wish it. Listen carefully. Within the catacombs are hordes of rats with a deadly poison in their bite. Once you are bitten, nothing can save you.	既然你堅持，那就仔細聽好。地下墓窖裡群聚著帶有致命毒性的老鼠。一旦被咬，便再無法可救。
If you are bitten, drink it and you will be cured. There is but one dosage, so waste it not.	你若被咬，飲下此物便能痊癒。這只有一劑份量，切莫浪費。
Go now. There is no turning back.	去吧，此去再無回頭路。
The way is open. Go.	通路已開，去吧。
There are three doorways.	這裡有三道門。
There are two doorways, mummies, urns and symbols upon one wall.	這裡有兩道門，其中一面牆上有木乃伊、甕與符號。
There are two doorways, a mummy, urns and symbols upon one wall.	這裡有兩道門，其中一面牆上有一具木乃伊、幾個甕與符號。
There is a round copper medallion around the neck of what may be the mummy of a child.	那具看似孩童的木乃伊頸間，掛著一枚圓形的銅製六角星項鍊。
There is nothing left but a pile of dust.	只剩下一堆塵土，別無他物。
The mummy in this niche is unremarkable.	這個壁龕裡的木乃伊平平無奇。
The mummy beneath the pentacle is quite small and has a medallion hanging around its neck.	五芒星下方的木乃伊體型頗小，頸間掛著一枚六角星項鍊。
The child's mummy has disintegrated, leaving only a pile of dust.	那具孩童的木乃伊已然崩解，只剩下一堆塵土。
Three of the walls are barren, but upon one wall there are two symbols painted.	三面牆空無一物，唯有一面牆上繪著兩個符號。
Two of the niches hold mummies, and two smaller niches are empty.	兩個壁龕裡供著木乃伊，另外兩個較小的壁龕則是空的。
One niche holds a mummy, and three others are empty.	一個壁龕裡供著木乃伊，其餘三個都是空的。
One symbol is a pentacle. The other is a labarum.	其中一個符號是五芒星，另一個是拉巴倫。
The pentacle, apples and the Goddess are often associated together because if one cuts an apple open lengthwise, he can find a five-pointed star hidden within.	五芒星、蘋果與女神常被相提並論，因為若把蘋果縱切剖開，便能發現裡頭藏著一顆五角星。
It is the symbol of Mithras, so we might assume that Roman soldiers once used these catacombs.	這是米夏拉的標識，由此可以推想，羅馬士兵或許曾使用過這處地下墓窖。
There are a great many bones around, as might be expected in catacombs.	四周散落著大量骸骨，在地下墓窖裡倒也不足為奇。
The funereal urns within these sepulchers are designed to hold the ashes of the deceased, or their mummified organs.	這些墓穴中的喪葬甕，是用來盛裝逝者的骨灰，或是他們製成木乃伊的臟器。
It is round, made of copper as best I can tell, and seems to have engraving upon it, but it is heavily coated with dust which obscures it.	據我判斷，它是圓形的，以銅製成，上頭似乎刻有花紋，但積滿厚厚的灰塵，看不真切。
I can tell you little about it until it can be clearly and closely seen.	在能仔細看清楚之前，我對它所知不多。
It is engraved with a pentacle and is imbued with a warding spell.	上頭刻著五芒星，並被賦予了辟邪的法術。
The medallion hangs around your neck beneath your tunic.	這枚六角星項鍊掛在你的頸間，藏於外衣之下。
There is no medallion here.	這裡沒有六角星項鍊。
Aye, but how, without risking a rat bite?	正是，但該如何取得，才不會冒著被老鼠咬傷的風險？
But you already took it.	但你已經拿到手了。
The trick is how to lift the medallion without risking a poisonous rat bite.	關鍵在於如何取下這枚六角星項鍊，同時不冒被毒鼠咬傷的風險。
What ARE you blathering about?	你到底在胡扯些什麼？
It is painted upon the wall.	它就畫在牆上。
It is too short and too blunt to do what you need.	它太短又太鈍，做不了你需要的事。
Very clever, Arthur! You have safely taken possession of the medallion.	真聰明，亞瑟！你已安全取得了這枚六角星項鍊。
Once more you are forced into a pitch black tunnel that leads in but one direction.	你再度被逼入一條漆黑的甬道，唯有一個方向可走。
It seems an eternity before the tunnel takes a turning and brings you to yet another hidden door.	彷彿過了永恆般漫長，甬道才終於轉了個彎，將你帶到另一扇隱藏的門前。
Push harder, Arthur! Aye, it opens as did the other one and returns you to the catacombs.	再用力推，亞瑟！沒錯，它如同先前那扇門一樣開啟了，將你帶回地下墓窖。
There are three doorways, mummies, urns and some symbols.	這裡有三道門、木乃伊、甕，以及一些符號。
Two walls contain niches of mummies and the two painted symbols. The other two walls are barren.	兩面牆上有供著木乃伊的壁龕與那兩個繪製的符號，另外兩面牆則空無一物。
Over one doorway is a small mushroom. Over the other doorway is the Gnostic symbol of the eight rayed sun.	其中一道門上方畫著一朵小蘑菇，另一道門上方則是諾斯替教的八芒太陽符號。
It is simply a small mushroom painted over one doorway. There are many mushroom cults in the Far East.	那不過是門上方畫的一朵小蘑菇。遠東有許多崇拜蘑菇的教派。
To the Gnostics, the eight rayed sun represents the universe with the dome of heaven in the center.	對諾斯替教徒而言，八芒太陽象徵著宇宙，中央則代表著蒼穹的圓頂。
Most of these mummies must be quite old, for they look dry and brittle, and smell of dust and decay.	這些木乃伊多半年代久遠，看來乾枯易碎，散發著塵土與腐朽的氣味。
This room now has three doors from which to choose.	這個房間現在有三道門可供選擇。
Now that the secret entrance is shut, there remain two doorways to choose from. The entire wall through which you entered is covered with a mural.	如今密道已經關閉，只剩兩道門可供選擇。你進來時經過的那整面牆上，都覆著一幅壁畫。
The air is stale and musty. Everything around you is covered with the dust of centuries. The mummies in their niches are ancient, untouched for ages.	空氣沉悶又帶著霉味。四周一切都覆著數百年的塵埃。壁龕裡的木乃伊古老不堪，多年來無人碰觸。
Would that Galahad had left some sign to guide us. He may be trapped in this foul place. Let us pray he is still alive.	但願葛拉漢曾留下什麼記號指引我們。他或許正受困於這污穢之地。讓我們祈禱他仍然在世。
But you must be extremely careful. I hear the skittering of the poisonous rats everywhere within the walls. Their evil eyes glint from behind and around the mummies. Avoid them at all costs!	但你必須萬分小心。我聽見毒鼠在牆壁四處竄動的聲響，牠們邪惡的雙眼在木乃伊四周與後方閃著光。無論如何都要避開牠們！
I can tell you this much, when you came down the stairs from the bazaar, you were facing north. Therefore the wall with the mural is facing south.	我能告訴你的是，當你從市集走下樓梯時，你面朝北方。因此那面有壁畫的牆，是朝南的。
There are two doorways from this room.	這個房間有兩道門。
There are now three doorways to choose from in this room. But the third one is not the same as the one through which you first entered.	這個房間現在有三道門可供選擇，但第三道並非你最初進來時經過的那道。
The secret entrance closed behind you. Your task, it would seem, is to discover a way out of here.	密道在你身後關閉了。看來，你的任務便是找出離開這裡的路。
Let us hope you will also discover some sign of Galahad.	但願你也能找到葛拉漢留下的什麼線索。
The tunnel and door which led you here are now irrevocably closed. Your choices are before you.	帶你來到這裡的甬道與門，如今已徹底封閉，再也回不去了。眼前的選擇就在你面前。
It shows the death of Adonis, one of Aphrodite's lovers. The legend is written in the Liber ex Doctrina.	畫中描繪的是阿度尼斯之死，他是阿芙羅黛蒂眾多情人之一。這段傳說記載於《Liber ex Doctrina》之中。
Interestingly, there is also a tree filled with golden apples in this mural.	有趣的是，這幅壁畫裡還畫著一棵結滿金蘋果的樹。
To learn more about the legend of Adonis, as shown in this mural, consult your Liber ex Doctrina.	若想多了解這幅壁畫所描繪的阿度尼斯傳說，可查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
The tree in the mural bears golden apples, a reminder of Aphrodite.	壁畫中的樹結著金蘋果，讓人聯想起阿芙羅黛蒂。
There are colourful, but meaningless patterns painted upon one of the doorways.	其中一道門上畫著色彩繽紛卻毫無意義的圖案。
He also would have entered here. Indeed, the dust on the floor looked a bit disturbed, but not enough to show which way he went.	他想必也是從這裡進來的。地上的灰塵確實看似有些被擾動過，但還不足以看出他往哪個方向去了。
That door closed securely behind you, leaving no trace that it was ever there.	那扇門在你身後牢牢關上，不留一絲曾經存在過的痕跡。
You cannot. A more powerful will than yours commands these doors.	你辦不到。掌管這些門的，是比你更強大的意志。
As before, the hidden door shuts as though it had never been there.	如同先前一樣，那扇隱藏的門闔上了，彷彿它從未存在過。
Nay, you have chosen wrongly! The door has shut behind you, trapping you within a pitch black hole scarcely larger than a coffin.	不，你選錯了！門在你身後關上，將你困在一個幾乎只有棺材大小的漆黑洞穴之中。
And a stone coffin it is, for here you shall die all too soon. Farewell, King Arthur.	而這確實是一具石棺，因為你不消多久便會死在此處。永別了，亞瑟王。
There is nothing worth seeing there.	那裡沒有什麼值得一看的東西。
Galahad's body lies upon the bier in what is now his own tomb as well.	葛拉漢的遺體躺在棺架上，此處如今也成了他自己的墓穴。
Galahad lies upon a bier within this chamber, surrounded by those long dead.	葛拉漢躺在這密室中的棺架上，四周環繞著早已作古之人。
He is in a healing trance	他正陷入療癒的恍惚之中
He is still alive, but deep in a fevered coma. He has been bitten and could die at any moment.	他還活著，但陷入了高燒導致的昏迷之中。他已遭咬傷，隨時都可能喪命。
Galahad has died because you failed to save him, though you had the means. His death is a black stain upon your soul.	葛拉漢已經死了，只因你明明有能力救他，卻未能出手。他的死是你靈魂上一道抹不去的污點。
Galahad is dead. Had you heeded the warnings of Fatima and the heirophant, this may have been averted.	葛拉漢死了。你若當初聽從法提瑪與祭司的警告，或許便能避免這場悲劇。
The low stone bier is covered by an old lion skin.	低矮的石製棺架上覆著一張老舊的獅皮。
Galahad's shield rests where he dropped it at the foot of the bier.	葛拉漢的盾牌就擱在他失手掉落之處，棺架的腳邊。
It is Galahad's sword.	這是葛拉漢的劍。
I do not know what gift Galahad wanted you to bring to Aphrodite, nor how you would do this. You will have to search for the answer to this riddle yourself.	我不知道葛拉漢想要你帶給阿芙羅黛蒂的禮物是什麼，也不知道你該如何辦到。這個謎題的答案，你得自己去尋找。
I do not know what "gift" you mean.	我不明白你所說的「禮物」是指什麼。
He will not answer. He is dead.	他不會回答了。他已經死了。
He is in a healing trance and cannot answer.	他正陷入療癒的恍惚之中，無法回答。
He is in no condition to answer you.	他此刻的狀態，無法回答你。
You have Excaliber. It is the only weapon you need.	你已有聖劍在身，那是你唯一需要的武器。
You have your own fine shield. It would be absurd to carry two.	你自己就有一面精良的盾牌，帶兩面實在荒謬。
It is made of stone and not going anywhere.	它是石頭做的，哪裡都去不了。
It is old and deteriorating and of no use to you.	它老舊又逐漸腐朽，對你毫無用處。
As the hierophant warned you, there is only enough for one use.	正如祭司警告過你的，這只夠使用一次。
If only you had not been such a fool and done as Fatima and the hierophant advised. Galahad is dead and you must bear the responsibility.	若你當初不曾如此愚蠢，聽從法提瑪與祭司的忠告該有多好。葛拉漢已死，你必須承擔這份責任。
It is too late. Had you acted in time, he would have lived. His death weighs heavily upon your soul.	為時已晚。你若及時採取行動，他本可存活。他的死，沉沉壓在你的靈魂之上。
This will serve as his tomb. Let him lie.	這裡便作他的墓穴吧，讓他安息。
He is just as well off here as anywhere. Better not to move him.	他留在這裡，並不比別處差。最好別移動他。
All hope is gone. Galahad is dead.	一切希望都已破滅，葛拉漢死了。
You have the means to save his life, if you have the courage to make the sacrifice.	你有能力救他一命，只要你有勇氣做出這份犧牲。
Galahad will live and revive eventually. Now you must go on. Your own life is at stake.	葛拉漢終將活下來、甦醒過來。如今你必須繼續前行，你自己的性命同樣攸關。
Alas, if you had but heeded the warnings of Fatima and the hierophant, perhaps you would have had a chance.	唉，你若聽從了法提瑪與祭司的警告，或許還有一線機會。
The rat's poison must be affecting your mind. You are babbling nonsense.	想必是鼠毒侵擾了你的心智，你正語無倫次地胡言亂語。
That is utter madness, to even think such a thing.	光是有這種念頭，便是徹底的瘋狂。
Ahem...do try to restrain yourself.	咳……還請你克制一下自己。
